sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: stage 6 of the command development pipeline. Each Node with the nested-fleet switch keeps the nested-fleet Project's default Instance, an Incus container that holds the inner fleet. After each Gateway release, Orbit deploys that default to the release commit, refreshes its fleet and takes the seed snapshot that a task or a new Instance of the Project clones. There is no VM, no image publish and no daily run. The per-Node run: docs/cli/instance/container/fleet-refresh.mmd. Until the last proof runs in containers, the task VM refresh (docs/cli/task/vm-image-refresh.mmd) still runs; see docs/reference/old-paths.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 6 · per-Node seed refresh
  %% kind: pipeline.6-task-image-seed-refresh
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=each Node tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=default tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>one run per Node
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>switched on
  participant C as Default<br/>with inner fleet
  Note over GW: Admit after a release<br/>best effort
  %%> Triggers:
  %%> - every verified Gateway release, from its admission step after Horizon starts; the release does not wait
  %%> When:
  %%> - a default with a clone copy in flight refuses with `instance.clone_in_flight`; the next release tries again
  %%> - a default with a deployment open refuses by its Instance lock; nothing queues behind it
  GW->>SW: Start one run per Node<br/>instance-deploy-direct
  %%> Why:
  %%> - each Node keeps its own seed; nothing is copied between Nodes
  loop each switched-on Node
    SW->>N: Keep the current seed<br/>before any change
    %%> Why:
    %%> - a failure then restores a seed that holds the fleet
    SW->>C: Deploy the release commit<br/>fetch · checkout · deploy steps
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the same steps as every container default deployment
    SW->>C: Refresh the inner fleet<br/>apply · converge · Doctor
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts the fleet, migrates the nested Gateway, converges the three nested Nodes, waits for Doctor
    SW->>C: Retake base<br/>fleet stopped
    %%> Why:
    %%> - a restore reverts device and config keys, so `base` holds every fleet rule
    SW->>N: Take the seed snapshot<br/>Processes stopped · ZFS
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - refuses when the Club key is a file on the default's disk; the key lives outside it
  end
  alt the run passes on a Node
    SW-->>GW: Node refreshed<br/>terminal event per Node
    Note over GW: Record the seed commit<br/>clones copy it
    %%> Result:
    %%> - one slow Node does not hold the others; existing clones keep their fleet
  else a step fails on a Node
    SW->>N: Restore the newest seed<br/>then start the default
    SW--xGW: Node not refreshed<br/>failed step
    Note over GW: Keep the old seed<br/>next release retries
    %%> Result:
    %%> - clones keep copying the old seed; the Operation names the failed step
  end
